{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "description": "Which pull request heads the local Claude review worker reviews (tools/claude-review-worker/worker.py), and how. every_pr reviews each same-repository, non-bot head; otherwise a head is reviewed when a changed file (or a renamed file's old path) matches an essential path glob (** crosses directories, * does not). visibility decides what is posted: a commit status on both, and one sanitized summary comment only on a private repository that the API also reports private. rules_files are read from main's copy into the prompt. A reviewed head is a trading change, and its prompt carries the upstream-alignment rule, when trading_every_pr is true or a changed path matches trading_paths (the trading lane's paths of docs/lanes.md; its adoption/manifest.json profile entries cannot be told apart by path).",
  "decision_record": "docs/decisions/2026-10-09-claude-review-worker.md",
